# Copy to .env.local for development.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is not a mistake: this value is compiled into the bundle and is readable by anyone
# who opens the app. That is fine — it is a URL, not a credential. Nothing secret belongs in an
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable, because there is no such thing as a secret in a client bundle.

# Where the API is. Required in every environment, including production.
#
# This used to say "empty in production", because the panel and the API were served from one origin
# behind Caddy and every request could be relative. That is no longer the deployment: the API
# answers on api.fitbase.com.tr and the panel on admin.fitbase.com.tr, so an empty value sends every
# call to the panel's own host, where nothing answers it. Build the panel with the API's URL:
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.fitbase.com.tr
#
# The refresh cookie survives the split and does not need SameSite=None. Those two hosts are
# different *origins* but the same *site*, and SameSite is a site-level rule — so the SameSite=Lax
# cookie still rides along. What the split does need is CORS, which the API registers from
# Cors__Origins__N; see the backend's Program.cs and .env.production.example.
#
# In development the Expo web dev server is on 8081 and the API on 5000. The API allows that origin
# by default only when running in Development.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000
